---
import Base from "../../layouts/Base.astro";
---

<Base
  title="Lead Path Kit Order Terms v1.0"
  description="Order terms for the one-time AI-Guided Lead Path Kit from Keith Staggers Studio."
  robots="noindex, nofollow"
>
  <article class="lead-path-terms">
    <div class="studio-shell">
      <header>
        <p class="studio-kicker">AI-Guided Lead Path Kit</p>
        <h1 class="studio-display">Order Terms<br /><strong>v1.0</strong><span class="text-signal">.</span></h1>
        <p>Version 1.0 · July 25, 2026</p>
        <a href="/lead-path-kit/">Return to the compatibility check</a>
      </header>

      <div class="lead-path-terms-body">
        <p>These terms are between the customer named in the order summary and Keith Staggers, a Florida sole proprietor operating as Keith Staggers Studio. The order-summary and Stripe invoice emails are the contact channels for the order.</p>

        <section>
          <h2>1. Order and price</h2>
          <p>The price is $149 USD, one time. Payment is due in full through a customer-specific Stripe invoice after the customer's reported setup fits one supported package. This screening does not test the live site or guarantee conflict-free installation.</p>
          <p>The order summary names the business, production website, platform, plan or version, theme or editor, installation path, rollback path, installer, contact action, delivery email, and delivery-timing rule. The exact delivery deadline is calculated when Stripe shows the invoice as paid and the intake is complete. The order begins only after both conditions are met.</p>
          <p>The compatibility approval and invoice remain valid for seven calendar days after invoice issue. If the invoice remains unpaid at the end of that period, it will be voided and no order begins. Reordering requires a fresh compatibility check, a new order summary, and acceptance of the current terms.</p>
          <p>Any legally required tax is the customer's responsibility and will be added only when Keith Staggers Studio is required to collect it.</p>
          <p>Version 1.0 is available only to customers with a United States business billing address.</p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>2. What is included</h2>
          <p>The order includes one made-to-order, electronically delivered package for one business, one production website and its staging or backup copy, one supported platform, and one primary contact action.</p>
          <ul>
            <li>Finished code for the confirmed platform.</li>
            <li>A platform-specific AI installation prompt.</li>
            <li>A start guide.</li>
            <li>Verification steps.</li>
            <li>Rollback or uninstall instructions.</li>
            <li>A package manifest.</li>
            <li>A package test report.</li>
          </ul>
          <p>The package is configured only with the confirmed business name, optional short services line, action type, action label, approved phone, email, or HTTPS destination, and primary color.</p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>3. What is not included</h2>
          <ul>
            <li>Site access or installation labor.</li>
            <li>Website redesign, theme work, copywriting, or revision rounds.</li>
            <li>Forms, lead storage, CRM, scheduling, payment processing, or integrations.</li>
            <li>Hosting, a subscription, license key, telemetry, analytics, trackers, or managed updates.</li>
            <li>New features or configuration changes after delivery.</li>
            <li>Work caused by inaccurate or incomplete intake information.</li>
            <li>Support for customer, contractor, or AI edits to the delivered code.</li>
            <li>Future compatibility with platform, plan, policy, theme, editor, browser, or third-party changes.</li>
            <li>A guarantee of traffic, leads, conversions, revenue, or business results.</li>
          </ul>
          <p>Requests outside this scope require a separate order, if offered.</p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>4. Customer responsibilities</h2>
          <p>The customer confirms that:</p>
          <ul>
            <li>They own the named website or are authorized to order for it.</li>
            <li>The website, platform, plan or version, theme or editor, installation permission, rollback capability, installer, and contact destination are accurate.</li>
            <li>The contact destination belongs to the named business or is authorized for its use.</li>
            <li>A backup, duplicate, or rollback point will be preserved before installation.</li>
            <li>The customer or an authorized webmaster will install, preview, publish, verify, and, if needed, roll back the package.</li>
            <li>No password, API key, recovery code, or private credential will be sent to Keith Staggers Studio or pasted into the AI installation prompt.</li>
          </ul>
          <p>The customer is responsible for site policies, accessibility obligations, privacy disclosures, professional rules, and legal compliance that apply to the customer's business and website.</p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>5. Delivery</h2>
          <p>The finished ZIP will be delivered through a Google Drive download link sent to the invoice email by the end of the next business day after both paid status and complete intake are confirmed. The deadline runs from whichever happens later.</p>
          <p>For these terms, a business day is Monday through Friday, excluding United States federal holidays, measured in Eastern Time. End of the business day means 11:59 p.m. Eastern Time.</p>
          <p>Delivery occurs when an accessible download link is successfully sent to the invoice email. A bounced message or inaccessible link is not delivery.</p>
          <p>The download link will remain available for 30 calendar days after delivery. The customer is responsible for downloading and backing up the ZIP during that period. The license does not expire when the delivery link is removed.</p>
          <p>The package is checked locally before delivery. Customer-site installation is not included and is not represented as completed. The customer must run the included live verification steps.</p>
          <p>If delivery cannot be completed by the promised date, the customer may choose a revised delivery date or a full refund.</p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>6. Cancellation and refunds</h2>
          <p>The customer may cancel for a full refund at any time before the package is delivered.</p>
          <p>Because the package is made to order and can be copied after delivery, it is not refundable after delivery for:</p>
          <ul>
            <li>A change of mind.</li>
            <li>Inaccurate or incomplete intake information.</li>
            <li>Inability or unwillingness to install the package.</li>
            <li>A request outside the order summary.</li>
            <li>A customer, contractor, or AI code change.</li>
            <li>A later platform, plan, policy, theme, editor, browser, plugin, or third-party change.</li>
            <li>A cosmetic preference that was not part of the confirmed configuration.</li>
          </ul>
          <p>This policy does not limit a right that cannot legally be waived.</p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>7. Covered defects</h2>
          <p>A covered defect exists when the original, unchanged package, installed as instructed on the accurately disclosed setup, reproducibly:</p>
          <ul>
            <li>Cannot be opened or is missing a file promised in the order.</li>
            <li>Fails a material step in <code>VERIFY-AND-ROLLBACK.txt</code>, including installation or activation, promised placement, primary-action destination, or rollback or uninstall.</li>
          </ul>
          <p>Installation mistakes that depart from the instructions, undisclosed incompatibilities, third-party conflicts, customer or AI edits, later platform changes, cosmetic preferences that still pass the included material verification steps, and requests outside the order summary are not covered defects.</p>
          <p>The customer must report a covered defect within 14 calendar days after delivery. The report should include the failed verification step and, when reasonably available, the page URL, screenshot, browser and device, and confirmed platform, version, theme, or editor. The customer must not send credentials.</p>
          <p>Within one business day after a defect report, Keith Staggers Studio will either confirm that the report is sufficient or send one consolidated request for missing non-credential evidence. The five-business-day correction clock begins when the requested evidence is received.</p>
          <p>Keith Staggers Studio will provide one corrected package within five business days after receiving sufficient information to reproduce a covered defect. The corrected package receives a new download link that remains available for 30 calendar days. The customer has five calendar days after corrected-package delivery to report that the same covered defect remains.</p>
          <p>If the covered defect cannot be corrected within the first five-business-day period, or the same covered defect remains and is reported within the five-calendar-day corrected-package period, Keith Staggers Studio will initiate a full refund to the original payment method within five business days.</p>
          <p>Stripe states that a refund typically appears at the customer's bank in approximately 5 to 10 business days. Bank timing is outside Keith Staggers Studio's control.</p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>8. Ownership and license</h2>
          <p>The customer keeps ownership of the business name, copy, colors, destinations, logos, and other material the customer supplied.</p>
          <p>Keith Staggers Studio keeps ownership of the generator, templates, shared component core, methods, documentation structure, and reusable code. No exclusive copyright or ownership transfer is included.</p>
          <p>After full payment, the customer receives a perpetual, worldwide, non-exclusive license to use and modify the delivered package for the named business on one production website and its staging or backup copy. The customer's employees and contractors may handle the files only for that permitted use.</p>
          <p>The customer may not resell, redistribute, sublicense, publish as a downloadable product, list in a marketplace, white-label, or use the delivered files or shared core to create products for another business.</p>
          <p>The customer may modify the files for the permitted website, but the covered-defect correction applies only to the original, unchanged delivered package.</p>
          <p>If a full refund is initiated, the license ends at that time. The customer must stop using and delete the original and corrected package files.</p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>9. Third-party platforms and AI assistants</h2>
          <p>WordPress, Wix, Squarespace, Shopify, GoDaddy, Google Drive, Stripe, browsers, themes, plugins, and AI assistants are third-party products outside Keith Staggers Studio's control.</p>
          <p>The included AI prompt may explain the instructions and guide the customer one step at a time. It may not rewrite or invent code, ask for credentials, change unrelated site settings, or claim success without the customer's live verification.</p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>10. Limitation</h2>
          <p>To the extent allowed by law, Keith Staggers Studio's total liability arising from this order is limited to the amount the customer paid for the order. Keith Staggers Studio is not liable for lost profits, lost data, lost leads, business interruption, or indirect or consequential loss.</p>
          <p>The customer remains responsible for backups, installation, publication, site operation, business decisions, and use of the delivered package.</p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>11. Data handling</h2>
          <p>Keith Staggers Studio uses the intake information only to check compatibility, prepare and deliver the package, keep transaction and delivery records, and handle a timely defect report.</p>
          <p>Payment information is handled by Stripe. Delivery is handled through Google Drive. Site credentials are neither requested nor accepted.</p>
          <p>Drive sharing is limited to the invoice email when practical. If the customer cannot access email-restricted Google Drive sharing, Keith Staggers Studio will request the customer's written consent before using an unlisted anyone-with-the-link Viewer link.</p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>12. Acceptance</h2>
          <p>Before an invoice is sent, the customer must affirm:</p>
          <blockquote>I confirm that I am the owner of, or authorized to order for, the named business. I confirm that the production website, platform, plan or version, theme or editor, installation permission, backup status, installer, and contact destination I supplied are accurate. I authorize work to begin after payment and agree to the AI-Guided Lead Path Kit Order Terms v1.0, including its scope, refund and defect policy, delivery method, and one-site license.</blockquote>
          <p>Acceptance must be affirmative and must not be preselected. The customer receives a retainable copy of these terms with the order summary.</p>
        </section>
      </div>
    </div>
  </article>
</Base>

<style>
  .lead-path-terms {
    min-height: 100vh;
    padding-block: clamp(4rem, 7vw, 7rem);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-rule);
    background:
      radial-gradient(circle at 82% 6%, rgb(40 81 255 / 0.15), transparent 28rem),
      var(--color-ink);
  }

  .lead-path-terms header {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) auto;
    align-items: end;
    gap: 2rem;
    padding-bottom: clamp(3rem, 6vw, 6rem);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-rule);
  }

  .lead-path-terms h1 {
    grid-column: 1 / -1;
    font-size: clamp(4rem, 8vw, 8.5rem);
    line-height: 0.82;
  }

  .lead-path-terms h1 strong { color: var(--color-cobalt); }

  .lead-path-terms header > p:last-of-type,
  .lead-path-terms header a {
    color: var(--color-paper-dim);
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.74rem;
  }

  .lead-path-terms header a {
    color: var(--color-signal);
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-underline-offset: 5px;
  }

  .lead-path-terms-body {
    max-width: 900px;
    margin-inline: auto;
    padding-top: clamp(3rem, 6vw, 6rem);
  }

  .lead-path-terms-body > p,
  .lead-path-terms-body section {
    padding-bottom: 2.4rem;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-rule);
  }

  .lead-path-terms-body section { padding-top: 2.4rem; }

  .lead-path-terms-body h2 {
    font-size: clamp(1.8rem, 3vw, 2.8rem);
    letter-spacing: -0.04em;
  }

  .lead-path-terms-body p,
  .lead-path-terms-body li,
  .lead-path-terms-body blockquote {
    color: var(--color-paper-dim);
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.82rem;
    line-height: 1.75;
  }

  .lead-path-terms-body section > * + * { margin-top: 1rem; }
  .lead-path-terms-body ul { padding-left: 1.25rem; list-style: square; }
  .lead-path-terms-body li + li { margin-top: 0.55rem; }

  .lead-path-terms-body blockquote {
    padding: 1.3rem;
    border-left: 3px solid var(--color-cobalt);
    background: rgb(40 81 255 / 0.08);
    color: var(--color-paper);
  }

  .lead-path-terms-body code {
    color: var(--color-paper);
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
  }

  @media (max-width: 700px) {
    .lead-path-terms header { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
    .lead-path-terms h1 { font-size: clamp(3.6rem, 16vw, 5.6rem); }
  }
</style>
